// 60 — Are the Layer 3 indicator blocks actually firing?
//
// Purpose      Layer 3 publishes indicators through the MDE Indicators API
//              (api.securitycenter.microsoft.com/api/indicators — the Graph tiIndicators
//              API is dead, removal April 2026). Creating an indicator and having it
//              enforced are different things. This query looks for evidence of enforcement.
// Tables       DeviceEvents, DeviceNetworkEvents, DeviceFileEvents
// Permission   ThreatHunting.Read.All
// Run          After indicators are published, and monthly thereafter.
//
// Indicator policy, for reference when reading the results:
//   * Malware domains (npm-cache.com, js-mirror.com, pypi-get.com) -> Block
//   * Ethereum RPC providers (eth-mainnet.nodereal.io, go.getblock.io, eth.llamarpc.com)
//     -> AUDIT, not Block. Legitimate use exists and blocking them is not proportionate.
//     Expect Audited events for these, never Blocked.
//   * 104.21.35.216 -> NOT indicator-blocked at all. Cloudflare shared address; blocking
//     it would take out unrelated services. Its absence here is correct, not a gap.
//   * The 7 payload SHA-256 hashes -> Block/quarantine as file indicators.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 — network indicator enforcement
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

let Blocked = dynamic(["npm-cache.com","js-mirror.com","pypi-get.com"]);
let Audited = dynamic(["eth-mainnet.nodereal.io","go.getblock.io","eth.llamarpc.com"]);
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where RemoteUrl has_any (Blocked) or RemoteUrl has_any (Audited)
| extend Policy = case(RemoteUrl has_any (Blocked), "should-block",
                       RemoteUrl has_any (Audited), "should-audit",
                       "unexpected")
| summarize Events     = count(),
            Devices    = dcount(DeviceId),
            ActionTypes = make_set(ActionType, 10),
            Processes  = make_set(InitiatingProcessFileName, 10),
            SampleUrl  = any(RemoteUrl),
            LastSeen   = max(Timestamp)
    by Policy, RemoteUrl
| order by Events desc
| limit 200

// Reading part 1:
//   should-block rows with a connection-success ActionType  -> indicator NOT enforced;
//       check that the indicator exists, is Block (not Audit), and that Network Protection
//       is in block mode rather than audit mode (coverage/04, coverage/05)
//   should-audit rows                                        -> working as designed
//   no rows at all                                           -> no contact attempts, which
//       is the expected steady state; it is not evidence of enforcement either way

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2 — file indicator enforcement, and AV/EDR detections naming this campaign
//
//   DeviceEvents
//   | where Timestamp > ago(30d)
//   | where ActionType has_any ("AntivirusDetection","AntivirusReport","SmartScreen",
//                               "ExploitGuardNetworkProtection")
//   | where AdditionalFields has_any ("Shai","Hulud","math_init","setup.mjs")
//        or FileName in~ ("math_init.js","Math_Symbol.js","setup.mjs")
//   | project Timestamp, DeviceName, ActionType, FileName, FolderPath, SHA256,
//             InitiatingProcessFileName, AdditionalFields
//   | order by Timestamp desc
//   | limit 200
//
// PART 3 — indicator inventory is NOT queryable here. To confirm which indicators exist,
// with what action and expiry:
//
//     GET https://api.securitycenter.microsoft.com/api/indicators
//
// Advanced hunting shows enforcement events, never the indicator list. An empty result in
// parts 1 and 2 is consistent with both "indicators published, nothing tried to reach the
// C2" and "indicators never published". Check the API before recording this as coverage.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
